    kind: invariant  # 6bb5
    title: "Two disagreeing generated-file predicates in supply_chain.py; the loose one classifies any 'Generated by' in the first 5 lines as DERIVED, which drops the file from analysis for Go but not for Python"  # 6bb5
    status: violated  # 6bb5
    priority: 2  # 6bb5
    parent:  # 6bb5
    tags:  # 6bb5
    - analysis_quality  # 6bb5
    - io_boundary  # 6bb5
    - go  # 6bb5
    isbefore: []  # 6bb5
    duplicate_of: []  # 6bb5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6bb5
    pr_ref:  # 6bb5
    description: "FOUND while extending scripts/measure-catalogue-reach.py to Go (see\ndocs/measurements/0002-catalogue-reach-multilanguage.md). The probe was excluding its\nOWN fixture and reported 0 of 210 Go primitives reachable; only the instrument's\npositive control (\"NOTHING RESOLVED ... refusing to report a 100% miss\") stopped that\nnumber from shipping.\n\nTWO PREDICATES, ONE QUESTION, DIFFERENT ANSWERS, in the same module:\n\n  supply_chain._GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN (line ~471) -- STRICT. Requires a\n    comment-prefixed line start AND one of: @generated, \"Code generated by ... DO NOT\n    EDIT\", Autogenerated, AUTO-GENERATED, \"automatically generated\".\n\n  supply_chain.is_likely_minified heuristic 3 (line ~822) -- LOOSE.\n    re.search(r\"(Generated by|@generated|DO NOT EDIT)\", head, re.IGNORECASE) over the\n    first FIVE lines, no comment prefix required, no extension gate.\n\nA file reading `// generated by scripts/measure-catalogue-reach.py` matches the second\nand not the first. The second wins, because classify_file consults is_likely_minified at\nstep 2 and returns Tier.DERIVED.\n\nMEASURED, identical body, only the header differing (Go, one file, two catalogued calls):\n\n    (no header)                                       -> 2 boundary calls\n    // leading comment                                -> 2 boundary calls\n    // generated by scripts/measure-catalogue-reach.py -> 0 boundary calls\n\nBisected to the phrase: \"// generated\" scores 2, \"// generated by\" scores 0.\n\nTHE ASYMMETRY IS THE SECOND HALF OF THE DEFECT. The same header on a .py file changes\nNOTHING -- probe.py with and without the identical banner both return 3 boundary calls.\nSo Tier.DERIVED suppresses analysis for Go and not for Python, and a user cannot predict\nfrom the classification what it will cost them.\n\nWHY THE LOOSE PATTERN IS TOO LOOSE. Go's actual convention is\n`// Code generated by protoc-gen-go. DO NOT EDIT.` -- the strict pattern's shape. The\nloose one additionally fires on any prose containing \"generated by\" or \"DO NOT EDIT\" in\nthe first five lines, which is ordinary in hand-written files (\"this table was generated\nby hand, DO NOT EDIT without regenerating\"). It also has no extension gate, so it reads\nthe head of every file it is asked about.\n\nDIRECTION: tightening the loose predicate makes MORE files analysed, which ADDS edges and\ntherefore adds findings. That is the recall direction and it is the expensive one to get\nwrong in the other direction (a genuinely generated 200k-line protobuf stub re-entering\nthe graph). Measure on a corpus with real generated code (kserve, cilium, containerd all\ncarry protoc output) before changing the pattern.\n\nNOT DIAGNOSED: which stage drops a Tier.DERIVED file for Go, and why the same tier does\nnot drop it for Python."  # 6bb5
    fields:  # 6bb5
      statement: "One question -- is this file generated? -- must have one predicate; and a file's classification must have the same consequence in every language."  # 6bb5
      root_cause: "supply_chain.py carries both _GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN (strict, comment-anchored) and is_likely_minified heuristic 3 (loose, case-insensitive, first 5 lines, no comment prefix). classify_file consults the loose one and returns Tier.DERIVED; the Go pipeline then drops the file while the Python pipeline does not."  # 6bb5
